  "hasSol": true,
  "task_html": "<div style='margin:10px 0 14px;'><iframe width='100%' style='aspect-ratio:16/9;border-radius:10px;border:none;display:block;' src='https://www.youtube.com/embed/m9SPKwJFRCE' title='Einsetzungsverfahren erklärt' allow='accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture' allowfullscreen></iframe></div><div style='background:#fffbeb;border:1.5px solid #fde68a;border-radius:10px;padding:12px 16px;margin:10px 0;'><p style='font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;margin:0;'><strong>Idee:</strong> Wenn eine Gleichung schon nach y (oder x) aufgel&ouml;st ist, kannst du diesen Ausdruck direkt in die andere Gleichung <em>einsetzen</em> &ndash; so bleibt nur noch eine Unbekannte &uuml;brig, die du normal ausrechnen kannst.</p></div><div style='background:#f8f8f8;border-radius:10px;padding:16px 18px;margin:12px 0;'><p style='font-size:13px;font-weight:700;margin:0 0 12px;color:#374151;'>Beispiel: &nbsp; (I) y = 2x+1 &nbsp;&nbsp; (II) 3x+y=16</p><div style='display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:flex-start;margin:8px 0;'><span style='background:#d97706;color:white;border-radius:50%;min-width:22px;height:22px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;'>1</span><span style='font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;'>y ist in (I) bereits isoliert: &nbsp;<strong>y = 2x+1</strong></span></div><div style='display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:flex-start;margin:8px 0;'><span style='background:#2563eb;color:white;border-radius:50%;min-width:22px;height:22px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;'>2</span><span style='font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;'>y in (II) einsetzen: &nbsp; 3x + <span style='background:#fef3c7;color:#d97706;font-weight:700;padding:1px 5px;border-radius:3px;'>(2x+1)</span> = 16</span></div><div style='display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:flex-start;margin:8px 0;'><span style='background:#2563eb;color:white;border-radius:50%;min-width:22px;height:22px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;'>3</span><span style='font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;'>Vereinfachen &amp; l&ouml;sen: &nbsp; 5x+1=16 &nbsp;&rarr;&nbsp; 5x=15 &nbsp;&rarr;&nbsp; <strong>x = 3</strong></span></div><div style='display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:flex-start;margin:8px 0;'><span style='background:#2563eb;color:white;border-radius:50%;min-width:22px;height:22px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;'>4</span><span style='font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;'>x = 3 in (I) einsetzen: &nbsp; y = 2&middot;3+1 = <strong>7</strong></span></div><div style='background:#f0fdf4;border:1px solid #bbf7d0;border-radius:6px;padding:6px 12px;margin-top:10px;font-size:13px;'>&#x2713; L&ouml;sung: <strong>(3&nbsp;|&nbsp;7)</strong> &nbsp; Probe in (II): 3&middot;3+7 = 16 &#x2713;</div></div><hr style='margin:16px 0;border:none;border-top:1px solid #ddd;'><p style='font-size:14px;font-weight:600;margin:8px 0;'>Jetzt du! Wende das Verfahren an:</p><div style='background:#eff6ff;border:1.5px solid #bfdbfe;border-radius:10px;padding:12px 16px;margin:8px 0;'><p style='font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;margin:0;'>(I) y = x+3 &nbsp;&nbsp; (II) 2x+y = 9</p></div><div style='font-size:13px;line-height:2.4;'>&#x24F8; y aus (I) in (II) einsetzen: &nbsp; 2x + <span style='background:#fef3c7;color:#d97706;font-weight:700;padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;'>(x+3)</span> = 9 &nbsp;&rarr;&nbsp; vereinfacht: 3x + 3 = 9<br>&#x24F9; x = <input class='cell-input' style='width:70px;display:inline-block;' data-ans='2' placeholder='?'><br>&#x24FA; y = x+3 = <input class='cell-input' style='width:70px;display:inline-block;' data-ans='5' placeholder='?'></div><div class='check-bar'><button class='btn-check' onclick='checkStation(5)'>&#x2713; &Uuml;berpr&uuml;fen</button><button class='btn-reset' onclick='resetStation(5)'>&#x21BA; Zur&uuml;cksetzen</button><span class='check-result' id='check-result-5'></span></div>",
  "sol_html": "<p style='font-size:14px;line-height:1.8;'>3x+3=9 &rarr; 3x=6 &rarr; <strong>x=2</strong><br>y=2+3=<strong>5</strong><br>Probe in (II): 2&middot;2+5=9 &check; &nbsp; L&ouml;sung: <strong>(2|5)</strong></p>",
  "mandatory": false
}
